{"title":"2024 CSMC Problems/Part B Problem 3 Part B","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CSMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_3\" title=\"2024 CSMC Problems/Part B Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CSMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=T-1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In the diagram, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> is a rectangle with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/5/235e58b6a077ef9b4e2372c3ea5b53ddbccffa59.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB &gt; BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"81\" height=\"13\" />. Point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/4/0948661e822f2a953c43a57ac9e40b2734476de4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> so that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/d/2dd985f15cc7042c5eed567ad214c710eefa646b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PD = PB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"85\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CSMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_3_Part_B&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CSMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_3_Part_B&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Suppose that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/0/e00f2adf9035f634ce10e2403ce21aab7e1922ba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB = 101$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"82\" height=\"14\" />. If the length of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> is an integer, prove that the length of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/d/b9d6394023b7f71962bce796b61343dcc276679c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PD$\" width=\"29\" height=\"12\" /> cannot be an integer.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CSMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_3_Part_B&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can suppose that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/d/b9d6394023b7f71962bce796b61343dcc276679c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PD$\" width=\"29\" height=\"12\" /> is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/3/ec397bfaefff48d5371bee4c2771545ced279085.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PB = PD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"85\" height=\"14\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/a/1ba7436927ee6026b08a6178a68d47271e1a4534.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PB = y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"65\" height=\"18\" /> as well. Opposite sides of a rectangle are equal to each other, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/5/a3573d72d2a5a2bb292812c79cb26c3c61bb39a6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD = AB = 101$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"136\" height=\"14\" />. This would mean that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/2/31207d90919d0d2a4c783549d5818d19d03382b8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PC = 101 - y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"114\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CSMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_3_Part_B&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>Using the quadratic formula, we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/a/8ba4878b7f35e63913c7be632cf92bbc0fafbe21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y^{2} = (101 - y)^{2} + x^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"164\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/6/aa69073d12d1d1477386df3f217a23b1cf9e4f72.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y^{2} = 101^{2} - 202y + y^{2} + x^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"216\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/0/2a04de09ac0ca9eb61ee24648e7d21ad938ed07b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-101^{2} + 202y = x^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"152\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/2/dc2a2ffc64640e9b0b21132b12f88b1f80d1e70c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$101(2y - 101) = x^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"153\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> is an integer, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/0/a400bcac50cfe083c42da4d5a9c2a9685ba7858b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2y - 101$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"70\" height=\"17\" /> would have to be an integer, meaning that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> would have to be divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/b/94bb6fb7a3ff722532798b45607025254679e7b2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$101$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/b/94bb6fb7a3ff722532798b45607025254679e7b2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$101$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> does <i>not</i> have any perfect square factors greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. However, this isn't possible because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/e/11e7980f7a9c3afc4fc7ac7d2252c8d0d8ee092d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB = 101 &gt; BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"135\" height=\"15\" /> and the side lengths cannot be non-positive.\n</p><p>Thus, this gives a contradiction, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> cannot be an integer. Therefore, if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/0/e00f2adf9035f634ce10e2403ce21aab7e1922ba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB = 101$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"82\" height=\"14\" /> and the length of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> is an integer, the length of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/d/b9d6394023b7f71962bce796b61343dcc276679c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PD$\" width=\"29\" height=\"12\" /> cannot be an integer.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018065813\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.020 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.037 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 121/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1451/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 5/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 5429/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   15.826      1 -total\n 87.12%   13.788      1 2024_CSMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_3\n 35.48%    5.615      2 Template:Image_needed\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:37466:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018065813 and revision id 289502. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}